   "id": "us-midterm-rally",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Wall Street rallies as Democrats take Congress and oil falls",
   "when": "Wed 4 Nov · New York session",
   "what": "The S&P 500 closed up 1.58% at 7,688.62 and the Nasdaq up 1.44% at 25,736.51. During the session Brent crude fell more than 9% to about $94 a barrel, and defence and oil stocks dropped while solar and healthcare shares rose. The 10-year Treasury yield ended about 6 bp lower. Tesla fell around 3% and Nvidia around 1% at midday.",
   "why": "The US is your largest group at about 25%. Investors are betting that a divided government means fewer new spending and war risks, which lowers yields and oil. This morning your dashboard prices ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) at their 2 Nov NAV, and the S&P 500 has risen 1.95% since, so that gain is not in your numbers yet. Tesla, a direct holding, was one of the weaker names.",
